<title>BRAZIL: Air mass poses no threat to Brazil coffee - Somar.</title>
<headline>Air mass poses no threat to Brazil coffee - Somar.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>A cold air mass which is expected to cause frosts in the far south of Brazil later this week poses no threat for Brazil's coffee regions, independent local meteorologists Somar said.</p>
<p>The cold front associated with the air mass will lead to isolated showers and cloudy weather in the coffee regions of Parana, Sao Paulo, the Cerrado and south Minas Gerais from May 22, Somar said in a regular weather update.</p>
<p>Temperatures in the north of Parana and south Minas Gerais should fall below 10 degrees Celsius but there is no frost forecast, it added.</p>
<p>Brazil's coffee regions face the greatest frost risk in the months of June and July.</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
